                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1fc6a0b-1c52-3eeb-9527-25a4ed0e2a05",
                        "entry_id": "02916973-5db8-3bac-84fe-b7398e0f4143",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vaste type de biome de savanes et de prairies inondables propre au bassin du Río Paraguay, couvrant près de 200,000 km² — ce qui en fait la plus vaste zone humide d’eau douce de la planète, et dont la biodiversité est très élevée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b728c4e8-2492-48ec-8f0d-110e6512b4a8",
                                "sense_id": "b1fc6a0b-1c52-3eeb-9527-25a4ed0e2a05",
                                "text": "Le voyageur qui a la chance de traverser le Chaco, la moitié occidentale du pays, est d’emblée frappé par la ligne ténue qui sépare le pantanal : 'marais', du désert proprement dit, …"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2e7d3c0-30ad-4ea7-a876-c69fc0961d49",
                                "sense_id": "b1fc6a0b-1c52-3eeb-9527-25a4ed0e2a05",
                                "text": "Au sol, le pantanal devient un paysage de rêve, où les troupeaux de zébus se réfugient comme sur des arches flottantes au sommet des buttes ; tandis que, dans les marais submergés, les bandes de grands oiseaux : flamants, aigrettes, hérons, forment des îles compactes, blanches et roses, moins plumeuses encore que les frondaisons en éventail des palmiers carandá qui sécrètent dans leurs feuilles une précieuse cire, et dont les bosquets clairsemés rompent seuls la perspective faussement riante de ce désert aquatique."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "85a9556a-e29f-37ec-9447-c1fcb7e860e9",
                        "entry_id": "02916973-5db8-3bac-84fe-b7398e0f4143",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Région précise où l’on retrouve ce type de biome."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "233d76f5-30fb-4549-99d1-c52cb64b5208",
                        "source_entry_id": "02916973-5db8-3bac-84fe-b7398e0f4143",
                        "target_lang_word": "pantanal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pantanal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85ac24cb-3a9a-32bf-b0fa-5a4c720147d3",
                                        "entry_id": "bf1286db-2bd4-38e8-800d-eedb8a0a6bab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A marsh (a broad, flat area with pools of water and trees) in the Pantanal region of South America."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "406bb909-2f55-4e9e-9110-f3dc3d4c545b",
                                                "sense_id": "85ac24cb-3a9a-32bf-b0fa-5a4c720147d3",
                                                "text": "To the west the savannahs extend as far as the affluents of the Paraguay and Madeira. Here, as on the coast, we come again to primeval forests, the 'pantanals,' of a tropical luxuriance, which, like the forests of Hylæa, owe their peculiarities to running water. To the south of these the plains of Gran-Chaco, and the woody highland of Paraguay, alternating with open grass[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de6909e7-07c9-4348-9d58-c0d79bc762fa",
                                                "sense_id": "85ac24cb-3a9a-32bf-b0fa-5a4c720147d3",
                                                "text": "Lepidosiren lives in the vast swamps (chacos and pantanals) of Rio Paraguay and Rio Amazonas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36c81690-c55d-4981-ab05-aa0fd4411834",
                                                "sense_id": "85ac24cb-3a9a-32bf-b0fa-5a4c720147d3",
                                                "text": "The land is largely composed of the pantanals, the flat, wide-stretching marshes through which the Paraguay and its affluents wind. Where the land is low it is covered with papyrus and water-grass; if a few feet higher , with open palm forest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "672a96ae-3c43-4b0e-bf78-377a5d9277fa",
                                                "sense_id": "85ac24cb-3a9a-32bf-b0fa-5a4c720147d3",
                                                "text": "Besides this, tourists are fascinated by the magic, enchantment and legends of the forests and pantanals and the natives are best indicated to narrate these stories in the authentic tone, suspense and mystery of the region."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96bb8860-6a9f-4519-b874-fb8776e794b0",
                                                "sense_id": "85ac24cb-3a9a-32bf-b0fa-5a4c720147d3",
                                                "text": "Diet seasonality and food overlap of the fish assemblage in a pantanal pond / Gisele Caroline Novakowski, Norma Segatti Hahn & Rosemara Fugi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ef51af1-ba5f-487c-9b39-19cba1af7c7b",
                                                "sense_id": "85ac24cb-3a9a-32bf-b0fa-5a4c720147d3",
                                                "text": "[…] sturdy bridges. Because of the Pantanals, there were no side roads and the bends were mostly gradual with no sharp turns. When confronted with oncoming traffic, unlike Robyn, Maxine planted her foot […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
